      theme: 'A census Yahweh commanded Himself, and a census that brought wrath — the same arithmetic, a different purpose, and the number struck from the record. An army cut down on purpose so no one could say mine own hand hath saved me. A comparison the Word calls not wise, and the measure distributed to us instead. The increase given rather than earned, the seed growing while the sower sleeps, and the house no labour builds without Him. A church that said it was rich and was not, and a name that lived while the thing was dead. A false balance that is abomination and a just weight that is His delight, with the plumbline held from outside the wall. And then the KPIs the Word already gave: fruit, occasions and days, faithfulness in the account, your own work proved, praise from another mouth, the ledger of sown against brought in, and sufficiency to finish.',
