        'A prophet who sat where they sat for seven days before a word was given him; a cupbearer who viewed the broken wall by night and told no man until he had seen it, and then said WE and US; a father-in-law who watched a whole day before he spoke, and whose first move was a question; an apostle of the same craft who abode with them and wrought, night and day, so as not to be chargeable; three friends who sat on the ground seven days and said nothing, which was the best thing they ever did for Job, and whose counsel afterward kindled wrath. Against all of it, the hireling whose own the sheep are not, and the man who answers a matter before he hears it. The pattern a newsletter is selling as new is the oldest pattern there is, because the Word was made flesh and dwelt among us. Nearness first. Counsel second. Never the other order.',
