    "bigIdea": "WHO TAUGHT THIS: NOBODY. No teacher, no recording, no Bible study. Gmail thread 1a1837bf55922f04 - a Supply Chain Connect send forwarded out of Darrell's university mailbox on 2026-10-28 at 17:08 UTC with one word typed above the forwarded header, Lesson., and then one item lifted by hand out of the body and set above everything else: 6 Steps to Better CFO-CPO Alignment, how procurement and finance can get on the same page about savings, spending and financial results. The subject line of the forward is about chip production and is NOT the ask; the lifted item is. Sixteen days stood between his word and this build. THE ARTICLE WAS NEVER READ, and that is said in every reader place: the email carries the headline and the one blurb and nothing else, and all three roads to the body were refused from this session - the publisher link would not resolve, and two publisher sites were refused by the network before a page was served. So not one of the six steps is taught here. What IS taught is the premise under the headline, tested against the Word and found older and larger than the framing: the one who buys and the one who counts have to be agreed BEFORE either of them can be right, and the Word says so with officers named, a dual-control procedure written down, and the reason given out loud. Can two walk together, except they be agreed. re-review: 2026-11-27.",
