    "inApp": "No new screens this week. What changes is one page you write by hand, and it takes about an hour. FIRST, write down the two offices in your own house - whoever decides what gets BOUGHT, and whoever decides what gets PAID and keeps the record. In a family that is often the same two people wearing different hats on different evenings; in a church it is frequently a trustee and a treasurer; on a rehab it is the person standing at the supply counter and the person reconciling the account. Name them, by name. SECOND, write the ONE number each of them is actually judged by. Not the number you wish they used - the one they really answer for. If one is judged by price obtained and the other by cash on hand at month end, you have found the misalignment without a consultant, because those two numbers can both improve while the house gets poorer. THIRD, write down where the two of them meet, how often, and who holds the book when they do. If the answer is nowhere, that is the whole finding. FOURTH, pick ONE purchase in the next thirty days and run it under 2 Kings 12:10 - two people see the money, together, and both set their hand to the count. Note what it cost in minutes. FIFTH, write the sentence from 2 Corinthians 8:21 at the top of the page and ask whether an outsider reading your record would call it honest in the sight of men, not only before Yahweh. If you cannot answer yes, you have next month's work. Bring the page to the person who handed you the project.",
